<title>USA: Bradlees to cut 105 jobs in restructuring.</title>
<headline>Bradlees to cut 105 jobs in restructuring.</headline>
<dateline>BRAINTREE, Mass. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bradlees Inc said Wednesday it has taken further steps, including cutting jobs, in its effort to reduce expenses and reengineer its operational structure to a more competitive size.</p>
<p>In conjunction with this reengineering, Bradlees said it will consolidate its two store management regions and eliminate about 105 positions at its central office.</p>
<p>Bradlees also said that, subject to bankruptcy court approval, it will close its store in New Hyde Park, N.Y., within the next several months.  The company cited the store's underperformance and disappointing sales results as the reason.</p>
</text>
